   "id": "us-ai-selloff-correction",
   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "US stocks slide into a correction as the AI trade unravels",
   "when": "Fri 20 Nov · US close",
   "what": "The S&P 500 closed down 3.70% at 6,910.42, its seventh straight daily fall. The Nasdaq lost 5.28% to 22,617.73 and the Dow fell 1.93%. The S&P 500 and the Dow now sit more than 10% below their record closes. Nvidia dropped 13.8% despite strong results and Meta fell 5.9%. Anthropic's shares gave back part of their debut gains. October inflation came in hotter than expected.",
   "why": "About 17% of your portfolio is in US large-cap funds. Both ES-US500RMF and K-USA-A(D) are priced at 19 Nov this morning, so the Friday fall is not in your dashboard numbers yet. The next refresh at 11:30 may bring newer fund prices. META is the largest single US stock hit, at 1.2% of your portfolio.",
